  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of solutions \\( n \\) to the equation \\( \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 \\) within the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\). We then need to determine how many of these solutions \\( x \\) make the graph of \\( y = f(x) \\) tangent to the \\( x \\)-axis, and find the value of \\( n + t \\).\n\n### Step 1: Solve the equation \\( \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 \\)\n\nThe equation \\( \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 \\) is satisfied when the argument of the sine function is an integer multiple of \\( \\pi \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[ 7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x) = k\\pi \\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is an integer. Simplifying, we get:\n\\[ \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine the values of \\( k \\) that satisfy the equation\n\nThe sine function takes values in the interval \\([-1, 1]\\). Therefore, \\( \\frac{k}{7} \\) must also be in this interval. This gives us:\n\\[ -1 \\leq \\frac{k}{7} \\leq 1 \\]\nMultiplying through by 7, we get:\n\\[ -7 \\leq k \\leq 7 \\]\nSince \\( k \\) is an integer, \\( k \\) can take any value from \\(-7\\) to \\(7\\), inclusive. This gives us a total of \\( 15 \\) possible values for \\( k \\).\n\n### Step 3: Determine the number of solutions \\( n \\)\n\nFor each value of \\( k \\), we need to determine the number of solutions \\( x \\) in the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\) such that \\( \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7} \\). The equation \\( \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7} \\) has two solutions in the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\) for each value of \\( k \\). Therefore, the total number of solutions \\( n \\) is:\n\\[ n = 2 \\times 15 = 30 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Determine the number of tangent points \\( t \\)\n\nFor the graph of \\( y = f(x) \\) to be tangent to the \\( x \\)-axis, the derivative of \\( f(x) \\) at these points must be zero. The derivative of \\( f(x) \\) is:\n\\[ f'(x) = 7\\pi \\cdot \\cos(5x) \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\cos(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) \\]\nFor \\( f'(x) = 0 \\), we need:\n\\[ \\cos(5x) = 0 \\]\nor\n\\[ \\cos(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 \\]\n\nWe already know that \\( \\cos(5x) = 0 \\) has two solutions in the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\) for each value of \\( k \\). Therefore, the number of tangent points \\( t \\) is:\n\\[ t = 2 \\times 15 = 30 \\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate \\( n + t \\)\n\nFinally, we need to find the value of \\( n + t \\):\n\\[ n + t = 30 + 30 = 60 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]",
